      "settings": {
        "summary": "Turn Claude Code into your client delivery system. Discover, scope, propose, onboard, build, review, launch, hand off and retain website clients with commands that read one set of files per client — evidence in every audit, counts in every scope, a range in every estimate, and a person between every draft and the client.",
        "button_label": "Get the Agency & Client Delivery System",
        "note": "One payment. Instant download. Licensed to one person for unlimited clients, including branding the client-facing documents as your own. Not legal or accounting advice."
      }
    },
    "walkthrough": {
      "type": "sbs-demo",
      "blocks": {
        "s1": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What lands in your inbox",
            "body": "One ZIP. Twenty-one numbered modules, 37 slash commands, 29 templates plus a client-project skeleton, 17 checklists, 12 report shapes, 3 worksheets, a reference set, four small scripts and a complete fictional engagement — about 56,000 words. Markdown, CSV, YAML; Python 3 standard library for the scripts.",
            "code": "claude-code-agency-client-delivery-system/\n  START-HERE.md\n  QUICK-START.md\n  01-lead-qualification/\n  02-client-discovery/\n  ...\n  21-client-offboarding/\n  .claude/commands/\n  templates/  (incl. client-project/)\n  checklists/\n  reports/\n  worksheets/\n  reference/\n  scripts/\n  examples/example-client-project/"
          }
        },
        "s2": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The first ten minutes",
            "body": "Copy the commands, scripts and templates into your agency folder; create the client project with the script (it never overwrites); fill the config from what you know; run discovery.",
            "code": "cp .claude/commands/*.md your-agency/.claude/commands/\ncp -r scripts templates your-agency/\ncd your-agency\npython3 scripts/new_client.py \"Northwind Supply\" --project \"Website Redesign\" --platform wordpress --type redesign\n  created clients/northwind-supply (28 files). Next: fill client-config.yaml, then /lead-qualification or /client-discovery\n\ncd clients/northwind-supply && claude\n> /client-discovery"
          }
        },
        "s3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Qualify before you spend unpaid hours",
            "body": "The intake is quoted, not paraphrased; a budget the prospect did not state stays blank. The score comes with reasons, the unknowns become the next call's questions, and WEAK means \"not on these terms\", not \"no\".",
            "code": "LEAD QUALIFICATION\n\nClient:   Harbourline Physio (director)\nProject:  Website redesign, WordPress, same domain\n\nFIT SCORE: STRONG\n\nProject Type:          Redesign; SEO preservation; booking conversion\nEstimated Complexity:  M\n\nUnknowns:\n- Which pages carry the organic traffic (Search Console)\n- Who holds hosting and registrar access\n\nRecommended Next Step:\nBook discovery; request Search Console/GA4 access first."
          }
        },
        "s4": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Audit with evidence, then scope from it",
            "body": "Every finding has an issue, evidence, business impact, recommendation, effort and a priority from CRITICAL to OPPORTUNITY. The priority actions become the candidate scope; the executive summary is two pages the client reads.",
            "code": "## Priority actions\n| # | Action                                        | Priority | Effort |\n| 1 | Booking CTA on every page; widget above fold  | HIGH     | build  |\n| 2 | Preserve the two URLs with 61% of clicks      | HIGH     | S      |\n| 3 | Rebuild templates for mobile (LCP 5.8 s)      | HIGH     | M      |\n| 4 | Unique titles; merge 4 thin pages with 301s   | HIGH     | S      |\n\nNot checked: server logs; the booking widget's own analytics."
          }
        },
        "s5": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A scope with counts and an out-of-scope list",
            "body": "In scope is counted (pages, templates, rounds, forms). Out of scope names what the client will think of later. Client responsibilities carry dates and the day-for-day rule. Every deliverable has a criterion someone can test.",
            "code": "IN SCOPE\n3. Design for the five page templates, desktop and mobile, 2 revision rounds\n4. Build as a child theme: 11 pages plus the profile template\n\nOUT OF SCOPE\n1. Copywriting beyond light drafts of titles/descriptions\n4. Online payments, deposits, or a client portal\n9. Maintenance beyond the 30-day defect window\n\nCLIENT RESPONSIBILITIES\n- Final copy for all 11 pages by 30 Oct; each business day\n  late moves launch by one business day"
          }
        },
        "s6": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "An estimate that is a range",
            "body": "Work items with low, expected and high hours and a note per row saying what each assumes. The script totals by phase, applies contingency as a line, and prints the assumptions. The proposal quotes the range or the high — never the low alone.",
            "code": "$ python3 scripts/estimate.py project-estimation.csv --contingency 15 --rate 90\nPROJECT ESTIMATE — 18 work item(s)\nphase              low  expected   high\nDesign            29.5      33.0   49.5\nDevelopment       30.0      34.5   50.0\n...\nTOTAL             95.5     135.8  205.2   hours before contingency\n                  95.5     156.1  236.0   with 15% contingency\nat 90.00/hour:    8595     14050  21243\n\nASSUMPTIONS (from the worksheet notes):\n  - Page assembly: 11 pages; assumes copy on time"
          }
        },
        "s7": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Scope creep, classified in a minute",
            "body": "Every new request is checked against the scope text — quoted, not remembered — and classified IN SCOPE, AMBIGUOUS or OUT OF SCOPE with the four impacts and the reply drafted. Not every change costs money; every change is logged.",
            "code": "REQUEST: \"Could clients pay for the assessment when they book?\"\nORIGINAL SCOPE: out-of-scope item 4 \"Online payments, deposits,\n  or a patient/client portal\"\n\nCLASSIFICATION: OUT OF SCOPE\n\nESTIMATED IMPACT: +10 to +15 business days before launch;\n  vendor add-on (client's) + 8–14h configuration; none if phase 2\nRECOMMENDED RESPONSE: /change-request CR-02; recommend phase 2\n  so the 9 December date holds."
          }
        },
        "s8": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The Friday report, from the tracker",
            "body": "Overall status with the one-sentence reason; completed, in progress, next week; the client's actions in their own section with dates and consequences; risks; decisions needed; the launch date and why it moved. Ten minutes from the files.",
            "code": "PROJECT STATUS — week of 2 November\nOverall Status: AT RISK — copy for three service pages is\n  outstanding since 30 October\n\nClient Actions Needed:\n  Approve design round 2            Fri 6 Nov   build starts Monday\n  Copy for the three service pages  Fri 7 Nov   launch 9 Dec holds\n\nLaunch target: 4 December → 9 December if the copy\narrives by 7 November (day-for-day rule)."
          }
        },
        "s9": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Launch on evidence",
            "body": "Thirteen checks with the file, the log entry or the test that proves each: scope, requirements, QA on the production build, written approval, backup, DNS, SSL, redirects, SEO, analytics, forms, environment, rollback. Any blocker is NO-GO regardless of the date.",
            "code": "LAUNCH RECOMMENDATION: GO WITH WARNINGS\nDecided by RL (recommendation) and the director (approval 8 Dec 16:20)\n\n| Client approval   | PASS | decision-log 2026-12-03; 8 Dec email |\n| Backup            | PASS | host 8 Dec 09:00; restore tested 2 Dec |\n| Redirects         | WARN | 4 rules staged; verified at T+15m |\n| Rollback plan     | PASS | previous theme kept; 15 minutes; RL |\n\nBlockers: none"
          }
        },
        "s10": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The whole engagement in one block",
            "body": "From the config, the tracker, the action items, the risks and the change log: phase, status, every stage, blockers, client actions, risks, the next five actions — and project-status.json for whatever you build on top.",
            "code": "$ python3 scripts/project_status.py --dir clients/harbourline\nCLIENT PROJECT STATUS\nClient:   Harbourline Physio\nProject:  Website Redesign\nCurrent Phase:   build\nOverall Status:  BLOCKED\n\nBLOCKERS:\n1. Copy for 11 pages (Content) is blocked on the client: 8 of 11 received\n\nCLIENT ACTIONS REQUIRED:\n1. Copy for Sports; Post-surgical; Workplace pages (due 2026-10-30) — overdue by 7 day(s)\n2. Approve design round 2 (due 2026-11-06)\n\nwrote project-status.json"
          }
        }
      },
